why The separate --cap-lints key is not visited in the current pinned successful inventory caller. Cargo f2d3ce0 add_cap_lints emits a cap only when show_warnings is false or is_local is false. Compiled units here are path-source and non-stdlib: checked fresh offline homes cannot provide fetched Git/registry units, no build-std route is supplied, and Unit::is_local is path-source and not is_std. Local units always show warnings, so both cap branches are false. Cleared environment, alias-only configuration, stable profile-feature gates, hard dynamic-target preflight and compile's lack of trailing rustc arguments exclude injected caps. Other operand consumers remain unchanged for this single table edit. Permanent actual-candidate controls require independent local producer argv/normalized outputs and refute a broader claim with successful cargo rustc -- --cap-lints allow: the changed helper leaks allow. Consumed-value and wrong positive/negative controls hold the scope. Source/caller proof and revalidation triggers: docs/specs/trust/flag-normalization-domain.md; changed producer/pin, package-source/stdlib/warning premises, environment/configuration/mode/arguments or consumers require revalidation. No arbitrary-argv or every-release claim (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.11.2.4.2).

