why The separate --color key is never visited in the current pinned successful inventory caller. Cargo f2d3ce0 add_error_format_and_color constructs joined JSON/error-format/width options and emits no separate color key. Compile supplies build or test/no-run with no trailing rustc args; cleared environment, alias-only configuration, checked fresh Cargo homes, stable profile-feature gates and hard dynamic-target preflight exclude injected flags. Fixed RUSTC=rustc also excludes replacement compiler programs. Other consumers remain unchanged per single edit, so any bare-key operand they consume is not visited. Changing this key's consuming bit therefore changes no output in that domain. Permanent controls compile this actual edit with independently expected ordinary argv/configuration. Plain Cargo color-plus-JSON refusal is not counted as a successful falsifier: a published test-owned RUSTC forwarding override provides successful Cargo builds and actual no-JSON compiler argv for always/never/auto. Raw requests and forwarded args are checked separately, real libraries consumed by an independent compiler, and variants retain each color operand outside the fixed caller. Consumed-value and wrong positive/negative/forwarded-argv oracles limit the claim. Source/premise/revalidation record: docs/specs/trust/flag-normalization-domain.md. Changed producer/pin, selector/formatter, arguments/environment/configuration/profile/preflight or operand consumers require revalidation; no arbitrary-argv or every-release equivalence (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.11.2.4.3.2).

from-json "if v.starts_with(\"metadata=\")"
to-json "if v.contains(\"metadata=\")"
why In the current pinned successful inventory caller, Cargo f2d3ce0 constructs the metadata operand with the literal metadata= prefix; it and the unchanged extra-filename=/incremental= operands are already discarded. All other visited -C operands come from Cargo constants or profile scalars accepted by Cargo/rustc and cannot contain metadata=. This includes strip: Cargo forwards a string, but rustc only accepts none/debuginfo/symbols; a rejected value makes run_cargo return before command normalization. Alias-only configuration and the cleared environment exclude linker paths and rustflags, stable feature gates exclude profile rustflags, hard preflight excludes build-script linker arguments, and build/test-no-run supplies no trailing compiler args. Other consumers remain unchanged and prevent operands from masquerading as visited -C tokens. Thus this single contains edit changes no result in that domain. Permanent controls compile the actual edit, assert literal real producer argv and normalized values, consume both produced libraries with value37, and refute wider equivalence with successful cargo rustc -C llvm-args=--pass-remarks=metadata=inside. Refused strip and synthetic key controls are explicitly outside the successful compiler domain; wrong argv/positive/negative/helper oracles fail. Source/caller premises and revalidation triggers: docs/specs/trust/flag-normalization-domain.md. Changed pin, constructors, arguments/environment/configuration/admissions/preflight or consumers require revalidation; no arbitrary-argv equivalence (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.13.2.4.2.1).

from-json "if v.starts_with(\"metadata=\")"
to-json "if v.starts_with(\"metadata\")"
why In the current pinned successful inventory caller, Cargo f2d3ce0 emits metadata= followed by its metadata value; no other Cargo-constructed visited -C key starts with metadata. Other codegen keys have distinct literal prefixes, and arbitrary rustflags/linker/build-script/trailing-argument routes are excluded by the checked environment, alias-only/fresh-home configuration, stable feature gate, dynamic-target preflight and build/test-no-run caller. Other consumers are unchanged, so source/cfg/path/extern operands cannot introduce a visited synthetic -C key. Removing this equals delimiter therefore changes no normalization result in that domain. Permanent controls compile this exact literal edit with independently expected actual Cargo argv/configuration, real libraries consumed with value37, valid wider LLVM input retained by this edit, and explicit metadataX=inside helper-boundary falsification of arbitrary-token equivalence. The synthetic key and compiler-refused strip are not valid successful-producer coverage. Wrong argv/positive/negative/helper oracles fail. Exact pinned constructors, successful scalar validation, caller premises and triggers: docs/specs/trust/flag-normalization-domain.md. Changed producer/pin, arguments/environment/configuration/admissions/preflight or token consumers require revalidation; no arbitrary-argv or every-release claim (leaf M3.6.9.6.3.2.2.13.2.4.2.1).
